{
  "name": "vector_light_differential",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "27 phase 3c. Four arms in ONE boot, because the question is a comparison and cross-run frame diffs on this mod already measure a 7-13 percent nondeterminism floor. Arms: vanilla, mask alone, the flat additive beam that ships today, and the differential beam. THE CLAIM UNDER TEST is that arm 3 lights the doorway like arm 2 while leaving the room like arm 1 -- the flat beam adds over the whole visibility polygon, and the polygon IS the lit region, so it lifts the room to 1.175x vanilla by construction. Arm 1 is load-bearing rather than decorative: it is the only arm that shows what the room looks like with nothing added, so it is what arm 3 has to match. vector_light_mask_available is pinned at 1 in every 27 arm because failing to read the per-emitter glow arrays is a defined STAND-DOWN rather than an error, and an unpinned arm photographs the crossfade while reporting a pass. ROOFED ON PURPOSE. The symptom was reported indoors, and roofing is load-bearing rather than set dressing: VectorLightOverlay.StrengthFor keys its daylight term on Roofed(emitter cell), so an indoor lamp runs at FULL strength at every hour while an outdoor one is attenuated toward zero by daylight -- which is why 0.5 read as acceptable outdoors and too bright indoors. It is also the only configuration where 7b's sky-cover alpha and 17's indoor gates are in play at all. THE ROOM IS ROOFED AND DOORED, taken wholesale from vector_light_open_door.json. A gap in a wall is an opening rather than a room, and the door is the point: it is the one place vanilla's flood is forced to detour, so it is the only place phase 3c is supposed to fire at all.",
